<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov chain store sales down 0.6 pct mth/mth.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov chain store sales down 0.6 pct mth/mth.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales at chain stores in Japan fell 0.6 percent in November from the previous month to 1.36 trillion yen, the Japan Chain Stores Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Chain store sales rose 0.2 percent in November on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>Sales of autumn and winter clothing and heating equipment were slow due to unusually high temperatures, the association said in a statement.</p>
<p>Sales of traditional year-end gifts were also sluggish, it said.</p>
<p>The November statistics covered 7,884 outlets of 132 companies, it said.</p>
</text>
